// The map_clock tick Low or High Level Alchemy may next be cast on.
//
// WHY A VARP AND NOT p_delay. Both alchemy labels used to end in p_delay, which is the engine's
// "this player is busy": while it holds, the server DISCARDS the player's walk clicks
// (MoveClickHandler rejects every one and unsets the map flag) and will not accept another spell.
// That is what made alching on the move impossible - not that the cast stopped you walking, but
// that every click you made for the next few ticks went nowhere, so a run across Varrock became a
// run that kept forgetting where it was going.
//
// A tick stamp enforces the same cast rate without telling the engine the player is busy, so the
// feet keep working and a premature click is simply ignored. One stamp covers both spells: it is
// the one spell delay in Old School, and casting Low after High does not dodge it.
//
// Temp, as map_clock is: it restarts with the world, so a stored tick would not survive one.
[alchemy_cooldown]
type=int
